  "problem": "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. $max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{11},\\mu )$\n\nII. $min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$\n\nIII. $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{11}}{{\\mu }^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}+1}$",
